{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the notification control flow and documented the causes in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n- `claude` was failing with `Not logged in · Please run /login`.\n- The script then assigned `$?` to zsh’s read-only `status` variable, aborting before either notification branch.\n\n`bin/nightly-review.zsh:19` now uses `exit_code`, preserving the agent’s exit status and allowing failure notifications to run.\n\nVerified both success and failure paths using local stubs, plus shell syntax and plist validation. No external service was contacted. The real job still requires Claude authentication; until then, it should send failure notes rather than reviews."}
